            "review_title": "Review at Luk Chew HongKong - Cha Chaan Teng",
            "review_text": "Nhi D\nHanoi, Vietnam23 contributions\n0\nOne of the best cantonese restaurants in HN\nJun 2019 • Friends\nI'd give this place 4 stars since it's probably the best Cantonese restaurants I've tried in Hanoi. The classic HK Milk Tea and the gooey condense milk bread were delish. The main dishes are okay: roasted charsiu and duck and fried beef noodles taste similar to the ones I had in China during the time I lived there, but less greasy (thank God). However, the eggplant casserole had a funny sour taste which I didn't expect and no shrimp paste :( Regardless, Luk Chew is still better than many other Chinese restaurants in HN ...\nRead more\nWritten June 16, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
